From c8d4a7a8c6919afde86367ab412d3328bbf5baa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mesh-LLM CI <ci@mesh-llm.local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:48:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek41: state the indexer views' geometry, and express a
 capped candidate count

Installing a stage program for any range reaching layer 2 failed in the proof replay.
Layers 2/8/14/20/24/28/32/36 are the indexer layers, so [0,2) never reached the code
and [0,40) always did:

    stage program VIEW geometry exceeds source storage for idx_q_rot-2 (view)
    source bytes=32768 dims=128x32x2x2 strides=4x512x16384x32768

span = 512 + 31*512 + 16384 + 32768 = 65536 against a 32768-byte source, exactly 2x.
dims[2] is the token axis divided by the stream count and was recorded as a constant.
Three more sites failed behind it: idx_k and comp_k, whose n_comp is the mask extent, and
the value tensor of the top-k mask's set_rows, whose row count is min(extent, top_k).

There is no separate "proof geometry" here. llama_model::build_graph either replays an
installed stage program or builds and captures one, so the first call captures -- the
reserve worst case, n_tokens=8 n_seqs=2 -- and every later call replays the real prefill.
A replay failure that is not "outside the recorded stage program control-flow domain" is
fatal, which is right: the fallback would be an un-sliced reserve, and that is the freeze
vector. So every runtime-dependent quantity in these graphs has to be expressible.

Five changes, all confined to the DeepSeek-V4/V4.1 family:

1. deepseek41 idx_q and idx_w state their geometry the way V4's indexer_q and
   indexer_weights already do -- tokens_per_kv_stream(), kv_stream_count(),
   source_stride_per_kv_stream(). The V4.1 port stated none of them.

2. deepseek41 idx_k and comp_k take their row count from source_dimension(0, 2), the axis
   of the tensor they view. dsv4_csa_extent()/dsv4_lid_extent() are the intended form and
   agree with it at capture, but a replayed program outlives the runtime values of the
   geometry it was captured under, and an extent read from the viewed tensor cannot
   overrun that tensor.

3. The replayed TOP_K count is clamped to the source extent. Every builder that emits
   TOP_K chooses min(extent, its own top_k) -- deepseek4, deepseek32, deepseek41,
   dots3note, glm-dsa and hy-v4 all do -- so the recorded count is already clamped to the
   capture extent, and replaying it verbatim against a narrower source trips
   GGML_ASSERT(a->ne[0] >= k) inside ggml_top_k and aborts the process. Re-applying that
   same clamp reproduces the value the builder would have chosen, and is a no-op for any
   model that replays at or above its capture geometry.

4. dsv4_csa_extent_capped/hca/lid(cap) express min(extent, cap), modelled on the existing
   tokens_per_sequence_capped, which carries its cap the same way. Additive: a model that
   does not opt in is unaffected.

5. build_top_k_mask derives the set_rows value tensor from top_k_3d, which already carries
   the clamped count, instead of from a ggml_new_tensor_4d scratch. A scratch becomes a
   ROOT of the program and a root records literal dimensions, so no geometry expression
   reaches one -- which is also why the dimensions[2]/[3] notes that were already on that
   scratch did nothing. A reshape to (1, k, ...) preserves the element count and a cast
   gives the value type, and both resolve from their source.

Note that ggml_cast is supported by the extractor: it is GGML_OP_CPY with no second
source, not an operation named CAST.

Verified on the real model, under a Job Object commit cap and a hard working-set ceiling:

    [0,3)   PLAN-OK  OPEN-OK  PREFILL OK  FRAME OK
            closure 44.203 GiB   peak_rss 0.664 GiB
    [0,40)  PLAN-OK  OPEN-OK  PREFILL OK  FRAME OK
            closure 246.344 GiB  ws_peak 3072 MiB  exit 0  elapsed 20 s

[0,40) is source and terminal, so it emits no activation frame (parts=0); that is the
single-node whole-model case, on a host with 15.69 GiB of RAM.

MESH_LLAMA_WS_BUDGET_MB still has to be raised to 12400 MiB to derive a valid n_ubatch.
That derivation has no lower bound and is not addressed here.
---
 src/models/deepseek4.cpp              | 39 ++++++++++---
 src/models/deepseek41.cpp             | 82 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/models/models.h                   |  6 ++
 src/skippy/stage_program.h            |  8 +++
 src/skippy/stage_program_geometry.cpp | 32 +++++++++++
 src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp   | 18 +++++-
 6 files changed, 176 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/models/deepseek4.cpp b/src/models/deepseek4.cpp
index 46b51b9..42761ac 100644
--- a/src/models/deepseek4.cpp
+++ b/src/models/deepseek4.cpp
@@ -857,6 +857,7 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_model_deepseek4::graph::build_lid_top_k(
 ggml_tensor * llama_model_deepseek4::graph::build_top_k_mask(
         ggml_tensor * kq_mask,
         ggml_tensor * top_k,
+        const skippy_stage_geometry_expression & rows_extent,
         const char * name,
         int il) const {
     GGML_ASSERT(kq_mask);
@@ -903,12 +904,34 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_model_deepseek4::graph::build_top_k_mask(
         skippy_stage_geometry_note(top_k_3d, geometry);
     }
 
-    ggml_tensor * zeros = ggml_new_tensor_4d(ctx0, cparams.flash_attn ? GGML_TYPE_F16 : GGML_TYPE_F32, 1, top_k_3d->ne[0], top_k_3d->ne[1], top_k_3d->ne[2]);
-    auto zeros_geometry = skippy_stage_geometry_static(zeros);
-    zeros_geometry.dimensions[2] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::tokens_per_kv_stream();
-    zeros_geometry.dimensions[3] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::kv_stream_count();
-    skippy_stage_geometry_note(zeros, zeros_geometry);
-    zeros = ggml_fill(ctx0, zeros, 0.0f);
+    // The value tensor needs one row per index, and a ggml_new_tensor_* scratch cannot provide one
+    // that follows: such a scratch is materialised as a root, whose dimensions are recorded
+    // literally, so the row count stays at its capture-time value while the indices follow the
+    // runtime one and the proof rejects the set_rows for the mismatch. A VIEW's geometry is
+    // evaluated, so take the rows from the mask, which is already expressed against the request.
+    // ggml_fill (not ggml_fill_inplace) keeps the value buffer distinct from the mask it views.
+    // The value tensor needs one row per index, and rows_extent states that count. A
+    // ggml_new_tensor_* scratch cannot carry it: the scratch is materialised as a ROOT of the stage
+    // program and a root's dimensions are recorded as literals, so no expression reaches it, which
+    // leaves the count at its capture-time value while the indices follow the runtime one and the
+    // proof rejects the set_rows below. Derive the shape from top_k_3d instead, which already
+    // carries the clamped count: a reshape to (1, k, ...) preserves the element count, and casting
+    // it gives the value tensor's type. A reshape's and a cpy's geometry are both resolved from
+    // their source, so the count follows the runtime.
+    ggml_tensor * zeros_shape = ggml_reshape_4d(ctx0, top_k_3d,
+            1, top_k_3d->ne[0], top_k_3d->ne[1], top_k_3d->ne[2]);
+    {
+        auto geometry = skippy_stage_geometry_static(zeros_shape);
+        geometry.dimensions = {
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::constant(1),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 0),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 1),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 2),
+        };
+        skippy_stage_geometry_note(zeros_shape, geometry);
+    }
+    ggml_tensor * zeros = ggml_fill(ctx0,
+            ggml_cast(ctx0, zeros_shape, cparams.flash_attn ? GGML_TYPE_F16 : GGML_TYPE_F32), 0.0f);
 
     ggml_tensor * kq_mask_top_k = ggml_set_rows(ctx0, kq_mask_all, zeros, top_k_3d);
     kq_mask_top_k = ggml_view_4d(ctx0, kq_mask_top_k,
@@ -994,7 +1017,9 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_model_deepseek4::graph::build_csa_lid_attention(
     cb(k_all, "csa_k_all", il);
 
     ggml_tensor * raw_mask = inp_attn->get_kq_mask();
-    ggml_tensor * csa_mask = build_top_k_mask(inp_csa.kq_mask, top_k, "csa_top_k_mask", il);
+    ggml_tensor * csa_mask = build_top_k_mask(inp_csa.kq_mask, top_k,
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::dsv4_csa_extent_capped(hparams.indexer_top_k),
+            "csa_top_k_mask", il);
 
     ggml_tensor * kq_mask = ggml_concat(ctx0, raw_mask, csa_mask, 0);
     cb(kq_mask, "csa_lid_kq_mask", il);
diff --git a/src/models/deepseek41.cpp b/src/models/deepseek41.cpp
index 7882cff..a375284 100644
--- a/src/models/deepseek41.cpp
+++ b/src/models/deepseek41.cpp
@@ -573,15 +573,77 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_model_deepseek41::graph::build_indexer_top_k(
     idx_k = ggml_view_4d(ctx0, idx_k,
             idx_k->ne[0], idx_k->ne[1], n_comp, idx_k->ne[3],
             idx_k->nb[1], idx_k->nb[2], idx_k->nb[3], 0);
+    {
+        // n_comp is a runtime extent, not a constant, so recording the capture-time value makes the
+        // view claim more rows than the tensor it views once that extent shrinks, and the proof
+        // rejects it for exceeding source storage.
+        //
+        // The extent is taken from the source's own axis 2 and not from a runtime extent
+        // expression. The measured LID extent (get_n_kv) is not this row count -- the cache's get_k
+        // slices it down before returning -- so expressing the view in terms of it re-introduces the
+        // overrun. Reading the axis from the tensor being viewed cannot: the view is a row slice of
+        // that axis by construction, so its span is bounded by the source's own storage.
+        auto geometry = skippy_stage_geometry_static(idx_k);
+        geometry.dimensions[0] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 0);
+        geometry.dimensions[1] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 1);
+        geometry.dimensions[2] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 2);
+        geometry.dimensions[3] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 3);
+        geometry.byte_strides[1] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride(0, 1);
+        geometry.byte_strides[2] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride(0, 2);
+        geometry.byte_strides[3] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride(0, 3);
+        skippy_stage_geometry_note(idx_k, geometry);
+    }
     cb(idx_k, "idx_k", il);
 
     const int64_t n_stream = idx_k->ne[3];
     idx_q = ggml_view_4d(ctx0, idx_q,
             idx_q->ne[0], idx_q->ne[1], idx_q->ne[2]/n_stream, n_stream,
             idx_q->nb[1], idx_q->nb[2], idx_q->nb[3]/n_stream, 0);
+    {
+        // Both views below divide a source extent by n_stream, so a recipe that records only the
+        // capture-time extents and strides describes a view that outgrows its source as soon as the
+        // token count at replay differs from the one at capture. The proof reads the recipe, not the
+        // tensor, and rejects it: "VIEW geometry exceeds source storage for idx_q_rot-*. (view)".
+        // The V4 indexer states these same two views in terms of the runtime stream geometry
+        // (deepseek4.cpp, indexer_q and indexer_weights) and V4.1 has to state them the same way.
+        auto geometry = skippy_stage_geometry_static(idx_q);
+        geometry.dimensions = {
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 0),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 1),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::tokens_per_kv_stream(),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::kv_stream_count(),
+        };
+        geometry.byte_strides = {
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride(0, 0),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride(0, 1),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride(0, 2),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride_per_kv_stream(0, 3),
+        };
+        geometry.view_offset = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::constant(0);
+        skippy_stage_geometry_note(idx_q, geometry);
+    }
     idx_w = ggml_view_4d(ctx0, idx_w,
             idx_w->ne[0], idx_w->ne[1]/n_stream, idx_w->ne[2], n_stream,
             idx_w->nb[1], idx_w->nb[2]/n_stream, idx_w->nb[3]/n_stream, 0);
+    {
+        // Same construction as idx_q above and the same latent defect: the extent on axis 1 is the
+        // token count divided by the stream count, and axes 2 and 3 divide source strides.
+        auto geometry = skippy_stage_geometry_static(idx_w);
+        geometry.dimensions = {
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 0),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::tokens_per_kv_stream(),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 2),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::kv_stream_count(),
+        };
+        geometry.byte_strides = {
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride(0, 0),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride(0, 1),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride_per_kv_stream(0, 2),
+            skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride_per_kv_stream(0, 3),
+        };
+        geometry.view_offset = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::constant(0);
+        skippy_stage_geometry_note(idx_w, geometry);
+    }
 
     idx_q = ggml_permute(ctx0, idx_q, 0, 2, 1, 3);
     idx_k = ggml_permute(ctx0, idx_k, 0, 2, 1, 3);
@@ -802,6 +864,20 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_model_deepseek41::graph::build_attention_v41(
     comp_k = ggml_view_4d(ctx0, comp_k,
             comp_k->ne[0], comp_k->ne[1], n_comp, comp_k->ne[3],
             comp_k->nb[1], comp_k->nb[2], comp_k->nb[3], 0);
+    {
+        // Same omission as idx_k above: n_comp is a runtime extent, not a constant, and the CSA
+        // extent reported by get_n_kv() is not this view's row count either. Read the axis from the
+        // tensor being viewed.
+        auto geometry = skippy_stage_geometry_static(comp_k);
+        geometry.dimensions[0] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 0);
+        geometry.dimensions[1] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 1);
+        geometry.dimensions[2] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 2);
+        geometry.dimensions[3] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_dimension(0, 3);
+        geometry.byte_strides[1] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride(0, 1);
+        geometry.byte_strides[2] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride(0, 2);
+        geometry.byte_strides[3] = skippy_stage_geometry_expression::source_stride(0, 3);
+        skippy_stage_geometry_note(comp_k, geometry);
+    }
     cb(comp_k, "comp_k", il);
 
     ggml_tensor * k_all = ggml_concat(ctx0, raw_k, comp_k, 2);
@@ -809,7 +885,11 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_model_deepseek41::graph::build_attention_v41(
 
     ggml_tensor * raw_mask  = inp_attn->get_kq_mask();
     ggml_tensor * comp_mask = top_k
-        ? build_top_k_mask(inp_comp.kq_mask, top_k, "comp_top_k_mask", il)
+        ? build_top_k_mask(inp_comp.kq_mask, top_k,
+                use_csa
+                    ? skippy_stage_geometry_expression::dsv4_csa_extent_capped(hparams.indexer_top_k)
+                    : skippy_stage_geometry_expression::dsv4_hca_extent_capped(hparams.indexer_top_k),
+                "comp_top_k_mask", il)
         : inp_comp.kq_mask;
 
     ggml_tensor * kq_mask = ggml_concat(ctx0, raw_mask, comp_mask, 0);
diff --git a/src/models/models.h b/src/models/models.h
index 90130c1..3078335 100644
--- a/src/models/models.h
+++ b/src/models/models.h
@@ -1388,9 +1388,15 @@ struct llama_model_deepseek4 : public llama_model_base {
                 ggml_tensor * inp_pos,
                 int il) const;
 
+        // rows_extent states how many rows the zero-filled value tensor carries. That count is the
+        // number of positions top_k selected -- min(candidate extent, the indexer's top_k) -- and it
+        // must be expressible: the scratch is built with ggml_new_tensor_*, so it has no source
+        // tensor for a relative geometry expression to resolve against, and a recorded constant
+        // leaves it at the capture-time count while the indices follow the runtime one.
         ggml_tensor * build_top_k_mask(
                 ggml_tensor * kq_mask,
                 ggml_tensor * top_k,
+                const skippy_stage_geometry_expression & rows_extent,
                 const char * name,
                 int il) const;
 
diff --git a/src/skippy/stage_program.h b/src/skippy/stage_program.h
index 1581f46..fc71a45 100644
--- a/src/skippy/stage_program.h
+++ b/src/skippy/stage_program.h
@@ -28,6 +28,11 @@ struct skippy_stage_geometry_expression {
         runtime_dsv4_csa_extent,
         runtime_dsv4_hca_extent,
         runtime_dsv4_lid_extent,
+        // The same three extents capped at a caller-supplied bound, for models that select
+        // min(extent, configured_top_k) candidates. Modelled on runtime_tokens_per_sequence_capped.
+        runtime_dsv4_csa_extent_capped,
+        runtime_dsv4_hca_extent_capped,
+        runtime_dsv4_lid_extent_capped,
         runtime_kv_stream_start,
         runtime_kv_stream_count,
         runtime_tokens_per_kv_stream,
@@ -68,6 +73,9 @@ struct skippy_stage_geometry_expression {
     static skippy_stage_geometry_expression dsv4_csa_extent(int64_t multiplier = 1, int64_t divisor = 1, int64_t addend = 0);
     static skippy_stage_geometry_expression dsv4_hca_extent(int64_t multiplier = 1, int64_t divisor = 1, int64_t addend = 0);
     static skippy_stage_geometry_expression dsv4_lid_extent(int64_t multiplier = 1, int64_t divisor = 1, int64_t addend = 0);
+    static skippy_stage_geometry_expression dsv4_csa_extent_capped(int64_t cap);
+    static skippy_stage_geometry_expression dsv4_hca_extent_capped(int64_t cap);
+    static skippy_stage_geometry_expression dsv4_lid_extent_capped(int64_t cap);
     static skippy_stage_geometry_expression kv_stream_start(int64_t multiplier = 1, int64_t divisor = 1, int64_t addend = 0);
     static skippy_stage_geometry_expression kv_stream_count(int64_t multiplier = 1, int64_t divisor = 1, int64_t addend = 0);
     static skippy_stage_geometry_expression tokens_per_kv_stream(int64_t multiplier = 1, int64_t addend = 0);
diff --git a/src/skippy/stage_program_geometry.cpp b/src/skippy/stage_program_geometry.cpp
index 0c5ba25..fb6d47c 100644
--- a/src/skippy/stage_program_geometry.cpp
+++ b/src/skippy/stage_program_geometry.cpp
@@ -136,6 +136,15 @@ bool evaluate_expression(
         case skippy_stage_geometry_expression::kind::runtime_dsv4_lid_extent:
             base = runtime.dsv4_lid_extent;
             break;
+        case skippy_stage_geometry_expression::kind::runtime_dsv4_csa_extent_capped:
+            base = std::min(runtime.dsv4_csa_extent, expression.constant_value);
+            break;
+        case skippy_stage_geometry_expression::kind::runtime_dsv4_hca_extent_capped:
+            base = std::min(runtime.dsv4_hca_extent, expression.constant_value);
+            break;
+        case skippy_stage_geometry_expression::kind::runtime_dsv4_lid_extent_capped:
+            base = std::min(runtime.dsv4_lid_extent, expression.constant_value);
+            break;
         case skippy_stage_geometry_expression::kind::runtime_kv_stream_start:
             base = runtime.kv_stream_start;
             break;
@@ -367,6 +376,29 @@ skippy_stage_geometry_expression skippy_stage_geometry_expression::dsv4_lid_exte
     return make_runtime_expression(kind::runtime_dsv4_lid_extent, multiplier, divisor, addend);
 }
 
+// Every indexer in this tree selects candidates with min(extent, its configured top_k), so the
+// number of selected positions is not a constant and not bare extent either -- it is whichever is
+// smaller at the geometry being resolved. A scratch tensor sized to hold those positions therefore
+// has no expressible shape unless the capped form exists. The cap is carried in constant_value, the
+// same way tokens_per_sequence_capped carries its own.
+skippy_stage_geometry_expression skippy_stage_geometry_expression::dsv4_csa_extent_capped(int64_t cap) {
+    auto result = make_runtime_expression(kind::runtime_dsv4_csa_extent_capped, 1, 1, 0);
+    result.constant_value = cap;
+    return result;
+}
+
+skippy_stage_geometry_expression skippy_stage_geometry_expression::dsv4_hca_extent_capped(int64_t cap) {
+    auto result = make_runtime_expression(kind::runtime_dsv4_hca_extent_capped, 1, 1, 0);
+    result.constant_value = cap;
+    return result;
+}
+
+skippy_stage_geometry_expression skippy_stage_geometry_expression::dsv4_lid_extent_capped(int64_t cap) {
+    auto result = make_runtime_expression(kind::runtime_dsv4_lid_extent_capped, 1, 1, 0);
+    result.constant_value = cap;
+    return result;
+}
+
 skippy_stage_geometry_expression skippy_stage_geometry_expression::kv_stream_start(
         int64_t multiplier, int64_t divisor, int64_t addend) {
     return make_runtime_expression(kind::runtime_kv_stream_start, multiplier, divisor, addend);
diff --git a/src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp b/src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp
index 1cd7b50..a6c7998 100644
--- a/src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp
+++ b/src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp
@@ -526,7 +526,23 @@ ggml_tensor * replay_operation(
             tensor = ggml_lightning_indexer(context, sources[0], sources[1], sources[2], sources[3]);
             break;
         case GGML_OP_TOP_K:
-            tensor = ggml_top_k(context, sources[0], operation_parameter<int32_t>(operation, 0));
+            {
+                // Every builder that emits TOP_K chooses k as min(the candidate extent, its own
+                // configured top_k) -- deepseek4, deepseek32, deepseek41, dots3note, glm-dsa and
+                // hy-v4 all do. The recorded k is therefore already clamped to the extent at
+                // capture, and replaying it verbatim against a narrower source trips
+                // GGML_ASSERT(a->ne[0] >= k) inside ggml_top_k, which aborts the process.
+                //
+                // Re-applying that same clamp against the replayed source reproduces the value the
+                // builder would have chosen at this geometry. It is a no-op whenever the source is
+                // at least as wide as it was at capture, so no model that replays at its capture
+                // geometry or wider changes behaviour.
+                const int32_t recorded = operation_parameter<int32_t>(operation, 0);
+                const int64_t available = sources[0] == nullptr ? 0 : sources[0]->ne[0];
+                const int32_t k = available > 0 && available < (int64_t) recorded
+                        ? (int32_t) available : recorded;
+                tensor = ggml_top_k(context, sources[0], k);
+            }
             break;
         case GGML_OP_CUMSUM:
             tensor = ggml_cumsum(context, sources[0]);
